  <h3 id="class-diagram">3.2 System Architecture & Class Diagram</h3>
  <p>The WIGMS system follows a modular architecture with clear separation of concerns. The main components include:</p>

  <div class="feature-box">
    <strong>Core System Components:</strong>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>AppState:</strong> Central state management structure holding all system data</li>
      <li><strong>Category Module:</strong> Guest categorization and management</li>
      <li><strong>Person Module:</strong> Individual guest registration and details</li>
      <li><strong>Seating Module:</strong> Table assignment and seating arrangement</li>
      <li><strong>Parking Module:</strong> Vehicle parking zone management</li>
      <li><strong>Gift Module:</strong> Gift registry and value tracking</li>
      <li><strong>Priority Module:</strong> Guest sorting and prioritization</li>
      <li><strong>Schedule Module:</strong> Event timeline and scheduling</li>
      <li><strong>UI Module:</strong> GTK+ interface components and event handling</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="diagram-placeholder">
    [CLASS DIAGRAM]<br>
    <em>Insert UML Class Diagram here showing system architecture</em><br>
    <small>Diagram should show: AppState as central class, Category/Person/Gift/Seating/Parking/Priority/Schedule as entity classes, UI_GTK as interface controller, with relationships and inheritance</small>
  </div>

  <p><strong>Key Class Relationships:</strong></p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Composition:</strong> AppState contains instances of all module managers</li>
    <li><strong>Aggregation:</strong> Category contains multiple Person objects</li>
    <li><strong>Association:</strong> Person linked to Gift, Seating, and Parking assignments</li>
    <li><strong>Dependency:</strong> UI_GTK depends on all business logic modules</li>
  </ul>

  <h3 id="use-case-diagram">3.3 Use Case Diagram</h3>
  <p>The system supports two primary user types with distinct use cases and permissions:</p>

  <div class="feature-box">
    <strong>Administrator Use Cases:</strong>
    <ul>
      <li>Manage Guest Categories (Create, Read, Update, Delete)</li>
      <li>Register and Edit Guest Information</li>
      <li>Manage Seating Arrangements and Table Assignments</li>
      <li>Control Parking Zones and Assignments</li>
      <li>Track and Manage Gift Registry</li>
      <li>Set Guest Priorities and Sort Lists</li>
      <li>Create and Manage Event Schedule</li>
      <li>Generate Reports and Statistics</li>
      <li>System Configuration and User Management</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="feature-box">
    <strong>Guest Use Cases:</strong>
    <ul>
      <li>View Personal Guest Information</li>
      <li>Check Seating Assignment</li>
      <li>View Parking Assignment</li>
      <li>Check Event Schedule</li>
      <li>Update Personal Details (Limited)</li>
      <li>Set Meal Preferences</li>
      <li>Update RSVP Status</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="diagram-placeholder">
    [USE CASE DIAGRAM]<br>
    <em>Insert Use Case Diagram here showing system interactions</em><br>
    <small>Diagram should show: Administrator and Guest as actors, with use cases grouped by module, inheritance relationships between use cases, and system boundary</small>
  </div>

  <h3 id="sequential-diagrams">3.4 Sequential Diagrams</h3>
  <p>The following sequential diagrams illustrate key system workflows and interactions between components:</p>

  <h4>3.4.1 Guest Registration Workflow</h4>
  <p>This diagram shows the step-by-step process when an administrator registers a new guest:</p>
  
  <div class="diagram-placeholder">
    [SEQUENTIAL DIAGRAM - Guest Registration]<br>
    <em>Insert Sequential Diagram for guest registration workflow</em><br>
    <small>Sequence should show: Admin → UI_GTK → Category Module → Person Module → Data Storage → UI Update</small>
  </div>

  <p><strong>Workflow Steps:</strong></p>
  <ol>
    <li>Administrator selects "Add Category" from UI</li>
    <li>UI_GTK captures form data (category code, guest count, guest details)</li>
    <li>Category Module validates data and creates Category object</li>
    <li>Person Module creates Person objects for each guest</li>
    <li>Data Storage saves category and guest information to .dat files</li>
    <li>UI_GTK updates display and refreshes tree views</li>
    <li>System updates statistics and notifies other modules</li>
  </ol>

  <h4>3.4.2 Seating Assignment Workflow</h4>
  <p>This diagram illustrates the process of assigning guests to tables:</p>

  <div class="diagram-placeholder">
    [SEQUENTIAL DIAGRAM - Seating Assignment]<br>
    <em>Insert Sequential Diagram for seating assignment workflow</em><br>
    <small>Sequence should show: Admin/Guest → UI_GTK → Seating Module → Person Module → Data Storage → Visual Update</small>
  </div>

  <p><strong>Workflow Steps:</strong></p>
  <ol>
    <li>User selects table and enters guest ID</li>
    <li>UI_GTK validates input and sends request to Seating Module</li>
    <li>Seating Module checks table availability and capacity</li>
    <li>Person Module verifies guest existence and retrieves details</li>
    <li>Seating Module creates seating assignment</li>
    <li>Data Storage saves seating information</li>
    <li>UI_GTK updates seating hall visualization</li>
    <li>System highlights assigned table and updates statistics</li>
  </ol>

  <h4>3.4.3 Parking Assignment Workflow</h4>
  <p>This diagram shows the parking zone assignment process:</p>

  <div class="diagram-placeholder">
    [SEQUENTIAL DIAGRAM - Parking Assignment]<br>
    <em>Insert Sequential Diagram for parking assignment workflow</em><br>
    <small>Sequence should show: Admin/Guest → UI_GTK → Parking Module → Person Module → Zone Validation → Data Storage</small>
  </div>

  <p><strong>Workflow Steps:</strong></p>
  <ol>
    <li>User selects parking zone and enters guest details</li>
    <li>UI_GTK sends assignment request to Parking Module</li>
    <li>Parking Module validates zone availability and capacity</li>
    <li>Person Module verifies guest VIP status for zone access</li>
    <li>Parking Module assigns specific parking spot</li>
    <li>Data Storage saves parking assignment</li>
    <li>UI_GTK updates parking yard visualization</li>
    <li>System highlights assigned spot and updates statistics</li>
  </ol>

  <h4>3.4.4 Gift Registry Workflow</h4>
  <p>This diagram illustrates the gift registration and tracking process:</p>

  <div class="diagram-placeholder">
    [SEQUENTIAL DIAGRAM - Gift Registry]<br>
    <em>Insert Sequential Diagram for gift registry workflow</em><br>
    <small>Sequence should show: Admin → UI_GTK → Gift Module → Person Module → Value Calculation → Data Storage</small>
  </div>

  <p><strong>Workflow Steps:</strong></p>
  <ol>
    <li>Administrator enters gift details and contributor information</li>
    <li>UI_GTK validates data and sends to Gift Module</li>
    <li>Gift Module verifies contributor exists in Person Module</li>
    <li>Gift Module calculates total gift value and updates statistics</li>
    <li>Data Storage saves gift information</li>
    <li>UI_GTK updates gift registry display</li>
    <li>System refreshes statistics dashboard</li>
  </ol>

  <!-- Section 4: Figma Design -->
